<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prasat Thong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1600–1656</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prasat Thong was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> from 1629 to 1656 and founder of the Prasat Thong dynasty. A senior official, he seized the throne after a series of palace coups, drove out the Japanese community whose soldiers had supported his rivals, and built the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wat-chaiwatthanaram">Wat Chaiwatthanaram</a>. His reign saw expanding trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prasat-thong.jpg" alt="Prasat Thong" width="224" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sun Colreone · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_King_Prasat_Thong.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
